title A merged weave deletes by name
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap under the baton, closing with a log, a commit, and the twice-pulled send.
rota lap 4450, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; the row asks what the work is for, and listening found a lap that had spoken and never been heard. The Lindy seat's ear rule -- a checked claim stays audible, an asserted one fades -- is exactly what separated the parked draft that had run from the parked drafts that only claimed.
obs Read the voice, the card whole, the fleet baton, the newest day shelf's top rows and its newest recommend line, and the aether triad -- the threshold, Follow Our Compass, The Lindy Effect, and The Grain and the Crossing.
obs The prior lap's recommend line pointed at the parked Mantra weave versions. Reading stash@{0} found more than a version: the 20260909-092428 round-open had stashed a WHOLE unsent lap, including its own session log at stamp 20260909.091106, which never reached the shelf. The card read as though this seat had last closed at 07:50, so the 09:11 lap was invisible from every living surface.
obs The stash base is 98ee0e0f91 and HEAD is 86cb4b9107, one commit ahead on a peer's design work. Nothing between those two commits touches mantra/ or the two tool paths, so the parked diff applied clean by git apply --check before any file moved.
file mantra/src/weave_merge_witness.rye recover prove_merged_weave_still_edits -- three lines whose document order reverses their identity order, one delete by LineId, the other two proven untouched by generation parity
file tools/fixtures/m/mantra_weave_merge_control.sh plant a binarySearch over the backing list in identity order, so the case has a break to catch
file tools/m/mantra_weave_merge_witness.rish require the new claim line and the new control phase; nine breaks becomes ten
file construction/ITINERARY.md shelve the elder account and carry this recovery with the parent Git nib
file construction/archive/20260909-151459_itinerary-landed-accounts.md hold the elder Patchouli account whole, its links re-anchored one level deeper
file session-logs/date/20260909/20260909-151459_a-merged-weave-deletes-by-name.kyri record the recovery, its provenance, and the load-bearing proof
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260909.md prepend this lap at its shelf-qualified address
obs The recovered case is proven LOAD-BEARING on this metal rather than assumed. With the case present the delete_lookup plant exits 134, which is 128 plus SIGABRT -- an executed assertion rather than a compile failure, since a build error exits 1 and the other planted breaks in this same control read 1 where they are compile faults. With the one call line removed from run_selftest and nothing else changed, the same plant exits 0. A refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass.
loom family=merge_delete_recovery plant_exit_with_case=134 plant_exit_without_case=0 control_readings=12 control_verdict=ok
obs The full control runs twelve phases and reaches control_verdict=ok: clean and bound_shrunk at 0 as the innocent legs, and ten planted breaks each caught.
obs weave.rye is untouched. The parked draft that ASSUMED identity-sorted backing storage was already refused by the 09:11 lap under REDS %636, and this recovery keeps that refusal -- it restores the regression case that pins the landed document-order implementation, never the implementation the case was written against.
obs TAME style bans read clean with its ratchets printed; width-check reads corpus_flagged_lines=1260 against a ceiling of 1260 and proves nineteen behaviors on planted repositories.
loom family=qa merge_rye=91 merge_rye_grade=A merge_control=85 merge_control_grade=B+ merge_rishi=80 merge_rishi_grade=B
obs All three touched artifacts grade B or better, so no molt frame was pushed. The three readings match the parked lap's own grades exactly, which is a small independent check that the recovered bytes are the bytes that lap measured.
obs I first decided to leave the parked log at 20260909.091106 in its stash, reasoning that its own status field reads verification and send pending and that landing it would put an unfinished verdict on the day shelf. The cold roster pass overruled that judgment by name: stash_record read unlanded=1 and printed the exact path, since a session log standing in a round-open stash with nothing else carrying it is what that guard exists to catch. The tree had already ruled on this shape, so the log lands with its pending status intact -- accrete-never-break protects a record written honestly mid-close -- and this log carries the verification that lap never reached.
file session-logs/date/20260909/20260909-091106_the-merged-weave-still-edits.kyri land the 09:11 lap's own record, its pending status kept as written
obs I moved the tree while the cold pass was still running, which the card forbids in plain words, so that pass read tree_moved=yes and cannot stand as this lap's cold reading. Its three reds are all downstream of that: tracked_link named the card's link to a shelf file I had written and not yet staged, stash_record named the parked log above, and standing_equipment is the roster's own self-check reporting the other two. The staged hot pass below is what measures the tree this commit ships.
loom family=standing_equipment phase=cold_invalidated guards_run=211 guards_green=206 guards_red=3 guards_gated=2 tree_moved=yes run_verdict=guard_red
obs All 30 stash entries remain, including the autostash. None was applied, dropped, or popped; the recovery read the parked diff through git diff between the stash and its parent and applied that patch.
recommend keep-going The merge and annotate halves of the weave both stand with witnesses; the next real work is the reader that shows what each side did across a merge, charted in the weave design. Before that, one lap should ask why a round-open stash can swallow a whole closed lap -- log included -- with nothing on any living surface saying so.
scope Recover the 20260909.091106 lap's merge-then-delete regression case, its control plant and its witness phase, prove the case load-bearing from both directions, and land it with the card and this log.
obs The staged hot pass ran 211 guards with 209 green, zero red, the two standing Pond custody gates, and tree_moved=no. tracked_link and stash_record both cleared once the shelf file was staged and the 09:11 log landed, and standing_equipment came green with them, which is the self-check reading its own roster whole.
loom family=standing_equipment phase=hot guards_run=211 guards_green=209 guards_red=0 guards_gated=2 guards_seconds=2343 guards_cpu_ms=2108518 tree_moved=no
obs The send met upstream twice. The first fetch was clean; between staging and the commit, xy moved two commits, one of them touching mantra/recall_tablecloth_query_delivery.rye. The rebase conflicted on one line -- the Git nib -- which I resolved to the new parent 23dee223dc, and I then caught my own typo in it, having written 23dee223d5 by hand where git prints 23dee223dc. The card's own pin_bound_touch guard refused the first amend at 136 bytes over 40960, since the rebase brought a peer's card growth with it; my own block condensed to fit rather than any other seat's.
obs A second re-integration followed: xy moved one further commit, 20f447ca1e, touching seventeen files and none of them under mantra/ or tally/. The nib moved with it and the merge witness ran GREEN again on that base.
obs Re-verified after the rebase: mantra_weave_merge is GREEN with ten breaks caught, and mantra_recall_tablecloth_query_wire -- the one guard watching the file upstream changed -- is GREEN too. The round's own files and upstream's do not intersect.
status GREEN -- mantra_weave_merge_witness passes with ten breaks caught; the plant exits 134 with the case and 0 without it; tame_style_check and width-check green. The staged hot roster pass and the dual send follow this written verdict.
